{templateType Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Styleguide\OverviewDefaultTemplate}

{*
 * How long things take, the curves they move along, and the loops a waiting
 * page plays. The list is FoundationTokens::MOTION.
 *
 * Nothing on this page moves for somebody who asked for reduced motion: the
 * rules in assets/base.css that animate the specimens are written inside
 * `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, like every other movement of the
 * design system. Without them the dots jump, and the loops stand still.
 *}

{import '../../templates/furniture.latte'}

{block sgPage}
    <p class="l-measure">
        A duration is a token with its curve; a component asks for what kind of change it is making - a
        hover, a disclosure unfolding, a layer coming in - and the theme decides how long that takes.
        Tick the box to move the dots, once along each duration and once along each curve; untick it to
        move them back.
    </p>

    <p class="l-measure">
        For somebody who asked for reduced motion, nothing here moves: the dots jump to the other end,
        and the loops stand still. That is how every movement of the design system is written.
    </p>

    <div class="sg-motion l-stack" data-testid="styleguide-motion">
        <label class="l-cluster">
            <input type="checkbox" class="sg-motion__toggle" data-testid="styleguide-motion-toggle">
            Move the dots
        </label>

        {foreach $motionGroups as $heading => $group}
            {include sgTokenTable, heading: $heading, kind: $group['kind'], tokens: $group['tokens']}
        {/foreach}
    </div>
{/block}
